<title>UK: Novorossiisk oil port shuts, Ventspils reopens.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk oil port shuts, Ventspils reopens.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Berthing at Russia's leading oil export terminal of Novorossiisk on the Black Sea was suspended on Tuesday due to a heavy swell, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port closed at 1000 hours local time. Two crude tankers were alongside berths one and six, loading from storage after the 660,000 barrels-per-day pipeline feeding the port was shut for 128 hours of maintenance work on Monday.</p>
<p>At 0600 local time on Tuesday there were about 766,000 barrels of crude in tank, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>Another small crude vessel was at anchor outside the port.</p>
<p>The Latvian port of Ventspils on the Baltic reopened on Tuesday after closing on Monday because of strong winds, the source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
